A||||9||p4n1c||Few 2.8 questions||||5||
Z||000000||p4n1c||12-20-2000||01:58 PM||||1) What makes the engine high output?<BR>   (Like the Fiero 2.8 puts out 140-<BR>    145hp, whereas the Beretta, Cutlass, <BR>    Firebird(or is this one HO too?), etc.   <BR>    2.8 puts out 125-130hp.)<P>2) Would you be able to take a newer 2.8 and <BR>   make it the same as the HO 2.8?<P>3) A question that goes along with #2 is how <BR>   hard would it be to use the power <BR>   steering from said cars?<P>4) Advantages/Disadvantages of DIS?<P>Thanks all   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>p4n1c<BR>Come out swingin'<p>[This message has been edited by p4n1c (edited 12-20-2000).]||||reg||5
Z||000001||ThatRickGuy||12-20-2000||03:16 PM||||1) What makes the engine high output?<P>The fiero 2.8 has the heads from the Camero/Firebird 3.4 as opposed to the standard 2.8 heads, better flowing and slightly higher compression.<P>2) Would you be able to take a newer 2.8 and <BR>make it the same as the HO 2.8?<P>I don't know of anything that uses a 2.8 other then old citations and s-10s. You can use a 3.4, redrill the starter holes, get the correct flex plat etc and it'll bolt right up.<P>3) A question that goes along with #2 is how <BR>hard would it be to use the power <BR>steering from said cars?<P>Theres a few people who have achived this and more people who are attempting. There was some talk about modifying an electric PS motor VS. mounting a pump in back and running the lines, just search the board for it.<P>4) Advantages/Disadvantages of DIS?<P>No idea, I thought it was only on the 4 bangers, so I never looked into it.<P>hope that helps<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||mshill||12-20-2000||03:16 PM||||#1 The heads are the differnce.  Larger valves get you the extra HP.<P>Don't have direct experience with #2,3,4.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||p4n1c||12-20-2000||03:29 PM||||A few cars use the newer 2.8(which uses DIS, automatic learned timing, etc).  '88-'89 Cutlass Supreme, '88 - '90 somthing Beretta and a few others.  The '86 Firebird uses the 2.8, but I think it's similiar to the Fiero one.<P>I will do a search on the power steering thanks.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>p4n1c<BR>Come out swingin'||||reg||1
Z||000004||terryk||12-20-2000||03:36 PM||||.<p>[This message has been edited by terryk (edited 12-20-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||p4n1c||12-20-2000||03:44 PM||||You're forgetting the W/L body cars(Cutlass(W), Grand Prix(W), Beretta(L), Corsica(L)) that used the MPFI 2.8 LO engine. I think the Sunbird used it as well, but I don't know the body code for them.  The 2.8 got around and is the most reliable engine that I've seen.  <P>Some guy didn't believe my dad when he phone for parts for our car and told them it was a 2.8.  He kept trying to correct my dad that it was a 3.1 when it says on the damn plenum that it's a 2.8 MPFI.<P>I find it is very underpowered for the cars they put it into(The Cutlass curb weight was around 3200lbs, with a 125hp 2.8.  Has some nuts, but not enough.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> ), but it has the reliability factor going for it(almost 400,000kms on my parents car).<BR><P>------------------<BR>p4n1c<BR>Come out swingin'||||reg||1
Z||000006||terryk||12-20-2000||09:57 PM||||If it's an injected 60 degree iron-head engine, it's an HO. Just the intake, exhaust, and ECM calibrations moved the HP around. The things that make them HO engines is the same. Once you get to the aluminum head engines, things change a bit.<P>Keep in mind that there is a certain amount of specsmanship going on. I'll bet the differences between the port injected engines (9,W,S) crank HP is not that much, if any. <P>Has the designation "High Output" been used on any 660 engine other than the Z code carburated engine? I don't recall any Fiero datasheets calling it an HO. Maybe I missed that.<P>DIS, disadvantage? Well, if it breaks, it's a bit more expensive with the crank and cam triggers and multiple coil packs. The amplifer is a bit expensive. Performance-wise, it's killer. Once you've had DIS, you never go back... Unforgiving to bad plugs and wires though. <P><p>[This message has been edited by terryk (edited 12-20-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000007||p4n1c||12-20-2000||10:50 PM||||Agreed with the unforgiving part for DIS.  We had a problem with the plugs not being torqued in enough and it was losing spark, the engine didn't like it. =]<P>Our battery died one time(should have been replaced long before it did), and I actually started our car with a lawnmower battery(never been used).  It started the car twice, boy did the car not like it.  It cranked over really, really hard and slow, then caught and the engine started.  I wonder why I love Olds so much(Chebby engine I know, but still  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> ).  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>As for the HO.  I just thought it might be, because of the 20hp difference between the normal 2.8 and the Fiero one.  I could be wrong with designating it as that.<BR><P>------------------<BR>p4n1c<BR>Come out swingin'||||reg||1
Z||000008||WKDFIRO||12-21-2000||06:26 AM||||DIS coil packs.<P>87 coupe automatic<P>243,311 miles.<P>One of the (original factory!!!) coil packs goes out. Changed only one, wanted to see how long the other one lasts...<P>Can't say they aren't dependable!<P>New engine at 253,000 miles, now at 265,000 (weekend car now, its done its time!)<P>LOVE those coil packs!<p>[This message has been edited by WKDFIRO (edited 12-21-2000).]||||reg||14
Z||000009||p4n1c||12-21-2000||08:47 AM||||I don't think my dad has ever changed the packs on their Cutlass.  I can't believe how reliable these engines are.  It's even taken a s*** kickin' from me when I was in high school.  I've calmed down slighty.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  Steve can tell you some of the stories.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  But I'm getting O/T.<P>What auto transmission is mated with the 2.8 in the '86 Fiero GT?  Any problems, things to be aware of with this transmission?<P>------------------<BR>p4n1c<BR>Come out swingin'||||reg||1
